Subject: [PATCH 11] bpf: mediate narrow HASH lookups with per-entry value authority

Base: patches 0001-0004, 0006, 0008 and 0010. Support one ordinary non-preallocated
HASH with u32 keys and 32-byte values. Retain an exact, data-only capability in
an aligned private entry trailer. The trusted allocation path supplies its
address; lookup never derives authority from a BPF-supplied address.

Read the key through the protected frame/access capability before entering the
Executive gateway. Pass only its scalar copy and return only the selected
value capability. Reuse the map-value access emitter and zero-permission RDDC.
Other helpers/profiles remain fail-closed. Map/RCU lifetime rules are still
required. Delay protected entry reuse until an RCU grace period so an active
non-sleeping invocation cannot hold authority to a newly assigned key. This
does not revoke capabilities held by an invocation after deletion.

